---
title: Capability-Gated Tool Registration
---
flowchart TB

  subgraph STATE["WORKSPACE STATE"]
    direction LR
    D["≥1 document indexed"]
    M["≥1 option AND ≥1 criterion"]
    H["≥1 score entered by the human"]
  end

  SEL["<b>selectCapabilities()</b><br/>{ documents, matrix, humanScore }<br/>memoised · recomputed only when the<br/>underlying slices change identity"]

  STATE --> SEL

  SEL --> REG["<b>syncRegistration(toolsFor(caps))</b><br/>diffs desired against registered<br/>· adds what is missing<br/>· removes what no longer qualifies<br/>· idempotent, so StrictMode is harmless"]

  subgraph ALWAYS["requires: [ ] — always registered"]
    T1["get_decision_state"]
    T2["list_documents"]
    T3["propose_criterion"]
  end

  subgraph DOCS["requires: ['documents']"]
    T4["locate_evidence ★"]
    T5["request_disclosure"]
    T6["read_snippet"]
  end

  subgraph MATRIX["requires: ['matrix']"]
    T7["explain_ranking"]
    T8["propose_score"]
    T9["attach_evidence"]
  end

  subgraph BOTH["requires: ['matrix','humanScore']"]
    T10["flag_inconsistency ★"]
  end

  REG --> ALWAYS
  REG --> DOCS
  REG --> MATRIX
  REG --> BOTH

  NOTE["<b>Why capabilities, not phases.</b><br/>A linear 0→3 sequence cannot express<br/>'matrix but no documents' or the reverse.<br/>Every branch required documents, so a fully<br/>populated matrix sat at phase 0 with one tool.<br/><br/>Each tool now declares what it actually needs."]

  REV["<b>Reversible by construction.</b><br/>Delete every document and `documents`<br/>goes false. The registry diffs against the<br/>smaller set and unregisters the three<br/>document tools. No ghost tools survive."]

  SEL -.-> NOTE
  REG -.-> REV

  classDef state fill:#ece0ff,stroke:#8050c0,color:#000
  classDef engine fill:#dce8ff,stroke:#4070c0,stroke-width:2px,color:#000
  classDef tool fill:#e0f5e6,stroke:#40a060,color:#000
  classDef note fill:#fff2d9,stroke:#c08820,color:#000

  class D,M,H state
  class SEL,REG engine
  class T1,T2,T3,T4,T5,T6,T7,T8,T9,T10 tool
  class NOTE,REV note
